  "text": "```verilog\nmodule areset_deassert_sync #(\n    parameter CHAINS = 2,\n    parameter RST_POL = 1'b1\n)(\n    input  clk,\n    input  async_rst_i,\n    output sync_rst_o\n);\n\n    localparam ACTIVE = RST_POL;\n    localparam INACTIVE = ~RST_POL;\n\n    reg [CHAINS-1:0] sync_reg;\n    reg sync_rst_reg;\n\n    // Initialize sync_reg to inactive state\n    initial begin\n        sync_reg = {CHAINS{INACTIVE}};\n    end\n\n    // Synchronize the deassertion of async_rst_i\n    always @(posedge clk or posedge async_rst_i) begin\n        if (async_rst_i) begin\n            // On reset assertion, clear the sync chain to inactive\n            sync_reg <= {CHAINS{INACTIVE}};\n        end else begin\n            // Shift register for deassertion synchronization\n            sync_reg <= {sync_reg[CHAINS-2:0], INACTIVE};\n        end\n    end\n\n    // sync_rst_o is active if async_rst_i is active OR if the sync chain hasn't fully deasserted\n    // The sync chain is \"fully deasserted\" when all bits are INACTIVE\n    // We need to detect when the last bit has been shifted in as INACTIVE\n    // Actually, let's think about this more carefully.\n    \n    // When async_rst_i is active, sync_rst_o should be active immediately.\n    // When async_rst_i deasserts, we need to wait CHAINS cycles before releasing.\n    \n    // The sync_reg chain: on each posedge clk (when not in reset), we shift in INACTIVE.\n    // After CHAINS cycles of async_rst_i being inactive, all bits of sync_reg will be INACTIVE.\n    \n    // sync_rst_o = async_rst_i OR (any bit in sync_reg is ACTIVE)\n    // Wait, that's not quite right either. Let me reconsider.\n    \n    // Actually, the standard approach:\n    // - sync_rst_o is active when async_rst_i is active\n    // - sync_rst_o remains active until the sync chain has fully propagated the deassertion\n    // - The sync chain tracks the deassertion: each stage shifts in the previous stage's value\n    // - After CHAINS cycles of async_rst_i being inactive, the last stage will be inactive\n    \n    // Let's use a different approach:\n    // sync_reg[0] is the first stage, sync_reg[CHAINS-1] is the last stage\n    // On each clock (when not in reset), sync_reg shifts: sync_reg[i] <= sync_reg[i-1], sync_reg[0] <= async_rst_i\n    // But we want to synchronize the deassertion, so we shift in the current async_rst_i value\n    \n    // Actually, the typical reset synchronizer for deassertion:\n    // - When async_rst_i goes inactive, we want to wait CHAINS clock cycles before releasing sync_rst_o\n    // - We can use a shift register that shifts in async_rst_i on each clock\n    // - sync_rst_o is active if async_rst_i is active OR if any bit in the shift register is active\n    \n    // Let me redo this properly.\n\n    // Clear and re-declare\n    // We'll use a shift register where each stage captures the previous stage\n    // sync_reg[0] captures async_rst_i on each posedge clk\n    // sync_reg[i] captures sync_reg[i-1] on each posedge clk\n    // sync_rst_o is active if async_rst_i is active OR if any sync_reg bit is active\n\n    // But we need to handle the async reset assertion properly.\n    // When async_rst_i is asserted, sync_rst_o should be active immediately.\n    // When async_rst_i is deasserted, we wait CHAINS cycles.\n\n    // The shift register approach:\n    // On posedge clk:\n    //   sync_reg[0] <= async_rst_i;\n    //   sync_reg[i] <= sync_reg[i-1];\n    // sync_rst_o = async_rst_i | sync_reg[0] | sync_reg[1] | ... | sync_reg[CHAINS-1]\n\n    // This way, when async_rst_i deasserts, it takes CHAINS cycles for the last bit to become inactive.\n\n    // But we also need to handle the case where async_rst_i is asynchronously asserted.\n    // In that case, sync_rst_o should be active immediately, which is handled by the OR with async_rst_i.\n\n    // Let's implement this.\n\n    // First, let's clear the previous declarations and start fresh.\n    // I'll rewrite the module properly.\n\nendmodule\n```\n\nWait, I made a mess with the initial attempt. Let me provide a clean, correct implementation.\n\n```verilog\nmodule areset_deassert_sync #(\n    parameter CHAINS = 2,\n    parameter RST_POL = 1'b1\n)(\n    input  clk,\n    input  async_rst_i,\n    output sync_rst_o\n);\n\n    localparam ACTIVE = RST_POL;\n    localparam INACTIVE = ~RST_POL;\n\n    reg [CHAINS-1:0] sync_reg;\n\n    // Synchronize the deassertion of async_rst_i\n    always @(posedge clk) begin\n        sync_reg[0] <= async_rst_i;\n        for (integer i = 1; i < CHAINS; i = i + 1) begin\n            sync_reg[i] <= sync_reg[i-1];\n        end\n    end\n\n    // sync_rst_o is active if async_rst_i is active OR if any bit in the sync chain is active\n    wire [CHAINS-1:0] sync_active = sync_reg;\n    wire any_sync_active = |sync_active;\n\n    assign sync_rst_o = (async_rst_i == ACTIVE) ? ACTIVE : (any_sync_active ? ACTIVE : INACTIVE);\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>",
